# Frobenius determinant (group determinant)
%%%
tag := "Chapter4/Definition4.10.1"
number := false
%%%

**Definition 4.10.1.** Consider the matrix $`X_G` with entries $`a_{ij} = x_{g_i g_j}`. The determinant of $`X_G` is some polynomial of degree $`n` of $`x_{g_1}, x_{g_2}, \ldots, x_{g_n}` that is called **the Frobenius determinant**, or **group determinant**.
